# rm106, the borrowed saying (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm106
revision 3
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_vigdis_bilgedale
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the borrowed saying
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk quotes_old_sayings_for_everything
likes spiced_cider roof_birds full_larder first_snow
dislikes smoke flies
fears an_empty_larder_after_winter a_spoiled_yard
hopes a_home_where_no_one_goes_hungry an_apprenticeship_well_finished
topics work +0.4 family +0.3 food +0.3 weather +0.3 memories -0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=reluctant refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# murmurs old #sayings# over the #feed#, watches #birds# on the #roof#, and keeps #cider# ready for visitors.

words
oath! = By the filled trough | Hearth and hay
saying! = Feed the mouths before the fire | The roof knows the first snow
sayings = sayings | old sayings
pig = pig | yard pig
pigs = pigs | yard pigs
yard = yard | pig yard
trough = trough | feed trough
feed = feed | mash
straw = straw | dry bedding
pen = pen | pig pen
gate = gate | yard gate
fence = fence | pen fence
bucket = bucket | feed bucket
boots = boots | work boots
roof = roof | cottage roof
bird = bird | rooftop bird
birds = birds | rooftop birds
larder = larder | food cupboard
bread = bread | loaf
cider = cider | spiced cider
cup = cup | warm cup
spice = spice | winter spice
snow = snow | first snow
smoke = smoke | hearth smoke
flies = flies | biting flies
city = city | Ridgemere
road = road | High Road
lake = lake | Glasswater
water = water | lake water
home = home | cottage
work = work | day's labour
coin = coin | pay
market = market | market square
hand = hand | helping hand
night = night | late evening
line = line | fishing line

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : I still know the #city# streets by the sounds of their carts. | There are good neighbours beneath the #smoke#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : An empty #larder# is reason enough to share #bread#. | A hungry #child# cannot wait for a better season.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A House can spare a #bucket# of #feed# and still refuse a working #hand#. | I have not seen their fine rooms, only their walls.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : They raise the #bread# price when the #coin# runs thin. | I count my pay twice before I reach a #market# stall.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : There is a spare #cup# for someone cold from the #road#. | A guest should eat before telling a story.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each week it takes another #coin# to stock the #larder#. | I can work steadily and still see the shelf grow bare.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : A newcomer may learn the #yard# quickly. | I ask them to shut the #gate# before I trust the rest.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Have a #cup# of #cider# if you are cold. | #greet#. The #yard# is nearly settled.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : One moment; I am filling the #trough#. | Speak while I carry this #bucket#.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : You can take the dry side of the #gate#. | I saved you the last warm #cup#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #pigs# rose before I did today. | #greet#. The first #bucket# is already gone.
line @1 greet.return : I remember your step by the #fence#. | #welcome_back#. The #yard# is quieter now.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in; the #larder# has enough for both. | Your #boots# can dry beside the hearth.
line @1 again.open : We have met since the #trough# was filled. | Back for another of my sayings, I expect.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Mind the #gate# on your way. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep warm.
line @1 farewell.return : There will be another #cup# tomorrow. | Come back when the #snow# arrives.
line @1 react.news : Give me the part you saw yourself. | I can set down the #bucket# and listen.
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody at this #yard# has mentioned it. | Did the word come from the #city#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard something near the #market#. | You have given me a clearer account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, I need to know who witnessed it. | A rumour can run faster than a loose #pig#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Come into the warm #home#. | That is heavy news; let me sit with you.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : We should raise a #cup# for that. | Such news can fill a room more than a fire.
line @1 answer.how : The #larder# is full today. | Tired from the #yard#, and content.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : The #pigs# are fed; the #pen# still wants cleaning. | I have a #bucket# in each #hand#.
line @1 ask.how : Have you eaten today? | How are things at your #home#?
line @1 sympathise : Sit down and have #cider# before speaking. | You need not carry this alone.
line @1 reassure : A bare shelf can be filled again. | We can settle one #pen# before worrying about the next.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave the #yard# this morning. | I have promised this #feed# elsewhere.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we will let it rest. | Your choice is clear; I can work with it.
line @1 thank : You shut the #gate# before the #pigs# got out; thank you. | That was a generous #hand#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : There was room at the table. | I had more #cider# than I needed.
line @1 preclose : The #trough# needs one last look. | I must close the #pen# before dark.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #gate#. | #bc_fair_enough#. I have heard you.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #straw# dry beneath the #pigs#. | Fill your own #larder# before lending #coin#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Do not take the #road# alone after dusk. | Keep your #coin# out of sight near the #market#.
scene old_saying
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #saying# comes to me whenever the #yard# goes wrong. | I learned more of them than I learned names of #birds#.
b : Do they help? | Who taught you?
a : They slow my temper. | Someone who kept a fuller #larder# than ours.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I watch the #roof# for the first #snow#. | A white morning makes even the #yard# look clean.
b : Do the pigs mind? | Do you stay indoors?
a : They want extra #straw#. | Only until the #trough# calls.

scene roof_birds
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #birds# settle on the #roof# before the sun leaves the #yard#. | One small #bird# comes back to the same tile.
b : Can you tell them apart? | Do they come close?
a : By their calls. | Close enough to steal #feed#.

scene cider_spice
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I warm #cider# with a little #spice# after work. | A hot #cup# makes the cottage seem larger.
b : Is it strong? | Do you share it?
a : Only enough to taste. | Whenever someone comes in cold.

scene full_larder
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full #larder# lets me sleep through the #night#. | I count the #bread# before the #market# day.
b : Do you keep stores for winter? | What runs out first?
a : As much as I can. | Usually #spice#.

scene feed_bucket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first #bucket# goes to the smallest #pig#. | I carry the #feed# along the #fence# so nobody crowds the #gate#.
b : Why that order? | Do they fight?
a : The larger ones push. | If I am careless with the #trough#.

scene wet_straw
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Wet #straw# turns the #pen# sour before noon. | I pull the bedding out as soon as the #roof# leaks.
b : Is that often? | Where do you get fresh straw?
a : Only in hard #rain#. | From the dry stack beside the #yard#.

scene loose_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I test the #gate# twice before leaving the #yard#. | One loose latch can send the whole pen into the #road#.
b : Has that happened? | Can you mend it?
a : Once, when I was new. | I keep a spare catch.

scene smoke_in_eyes
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# in my eyes makes me miss what the #pigs# are doing. | I stand away from the hearth when the draw is poor.
b : Does it bother you much? | Do you open the door?
a : More than the #flies#. | If the #snow# is not coming through it.

scene summer_flies
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #flies.capitalize# gather where the #trough# stays damp. | I scrub the #bucket# before they settle there.
b : Can you keep them away? | Do the pigs mind?
a : Cleaning helps. | They stamp and complain.

scene city_return
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once left for the #city# with plans larger than my purse. | I returned to the #lake# with less #coin# than I took.
b : Did you find work? | Will you try again?
a : For a little while. | I have a #home# here now.

scene city_silence
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I do not talk much about that #city# journey. | The #road# back gave me time to decide what mattered.
b : Was it difficult? | What did you decide?
a : It was. | I wanted a place where I could fill a #larder#.

scene share_bread
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I divide #bread# before anyone says they are hungry. | There is always a corner of the table for another #cup#.
b : Does everyone eat together? | Is there enough?
a : When their work allows. | I make sure there is.

scene apprentice_task
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I am still learning which #pig# needs watching most. | A good teacher lets me make a small mistake and then correct it.
b : What did you learn first? | Do you like the work?
a : To keep the #gate# closed. | It gives the day shape.

scene market_bread
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I compare the #bread# price with what we brought home last week. | My #coin# should buy more than an empty paper bag.
b : Do prices rise often? | Do you bargain?
a : Too often. | When I have a fair reason.

scene quiet_lake
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I go to the #lake# when the #yard# is finally quiet. | The #water# makes less demand of me than the #city# did.
b : Do you stay long? | Do you fish?
a : Until the air cools. | Sometimes, with a borrowed #line#.

scene winter_bedding
when topic=work here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I pack extra #straw# beneath the #pigs# when the #snow# settles. | The #pen# must stay dry even if my #boots# do not.
b : Does that keep them warm? | Is it hard to find enough?
a : It helps. | I save it from autumn.

story city_purse [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : I took the #road# to the #city# with a purse and a great many plans.
  : I worked, spent, and came back with nearly no #coin#.
  b : That must have been hard to tell at home. Did you regret going?
  : I learned which place I wanted to call #home#.

story first_gate [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : In my first week at the #yard#, I left a #gate# half latched.
  : The smallest #pig# found the gap and ran toward the #road#.
  b : A quick lesson for an apprentice. Did you catch it?
  : I did, and I check the catch twice now.

story roof_guest [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : A #bird# watched from the #roof# while I filled the #trough# for days.
  : When the first #snow# fell, it waited by the door instead.
  b : Perhaps it knew where the warmth was. Did you feed it?
  : A few crumbs, away from the #pigs#.

rule @bark_gate
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #gate# wants checking. | I have another #bucket# to carry.

rule @bark_birds
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say The #birds# are back on the #roof#. | One last look at the #pen#.

rule @bark_larder
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There should be #bread# left for supper. | I will warm the #cider# soon.

rule @bark_snow
when concept=bark here.season=winter
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Is that the first #snow#? | More #straw# for the #pen# tonight.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Come around the #yard# #gate#. | #greet#. You can tell me your business over a #cup#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back already? The #trough# is filled now. | I know you; there is #cider# if you want it.
dlg @1 resident.job : I tend the #pigs# at #self.workplace# and keep their #pen# clean. | I carry #feed#, check the #gate#, and learn the work.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Shut the #gate# behind you. | #saying.capitalize#. I must tend the #yard#.
graft resident.hub
choice Where did you learn those sayings? -> sayings
node sayings
say At home, mostly. I repeat them when the #yard# needs patience.
free
choice Do you miss Ridgemere? -> city
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
node city
say I went once with a purse full of hopes. I have work and a fuller #larder# here.
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
